  Okay, this subject has been beaten to death, one last bleat and I'll
shut up about it.

  First, it's easy to get a poly wand:  all you have to do is choose
to play a wizard, and reroll 50-100 times, and eventually you'll be
given one.
  Even then, the game is not necessarily easy.  You have to survive the
first ten or so levels, kill a bunch of orcs to get their weapons and
armor, and collect as much junk as you can, and you have to find a
lawful altar.  
  But once you've done those things, the game is a gimme.

  A truly excellent computer game is one that remains difficult but
playable throughout its whole course.  Nethack has made great strides
toward becoming an excellent game -- all that remains is to remove
the few loopholes.  Poly-wanding is one; the method of using wands of
wishing to create more wands of wishing is another; maybe the ring of
conflict is also one, though I'm not sure of that.

